ers/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":740487,"digest":"sha256:56dacb6d89686cea9d8dfae89bb52e7686ee736aea75f7fde3a6df7018510f43","download_count":9,"created_at":"2026-10-12T20:15:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T20:15:35Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/releases/download/v8.4.176/sbom.spdx.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ultralytics/ultralytics/tarball/v8.4.176","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ultralytics/ultralytics/zipball/v8.4.176","body":"## 🌟 Summary\nYOLO 8.4.176 makes YOLO-World checkpoints much smaller after setting custom classes, while improving reliability across validation, fine-tuning, segmentation, tracking, and model deployment.\n\n## 📊 Key Changes\n- **YOLO-World checkpoints are dramatically smaller:** Setting classes no longer caches the CLIP text encoder by default. For `yolov8s-worldv2.pt`, a saved checkpoint shrank from **328.5 MB to 25.8 MB**, with identical predictions after reload. Caching remains available when explicitly requested.\n- **More reliable validation and fine-tuning:** Detection validation now matches predictions to eligible targets in confidence order, reducing missed matches. YOLOE fine-tuning and resume also preserve trained classification heads instead of reinitializing them.\n- **Fixes for segmentation and SAM:** MobileSAM FP16 inference no longer produces empty masks. Reused SAM predictors now reset state for new images and videos. A mask-thresholding change was reverted after it reduced YOLO26 segmentation mAP.\n- **Improved deployment and input handling:** ONNX GPU inference now supports custom input names and strided tensors; OpenVINO NPU inference handles batches and depth outputs more reliably. Floating-point NumPy images also work with grayscale models.\n- **Smoother video, tracking, and benchmarking:** Saved videos preserve fractional frame rates, high-FPS streams are handled correctly, and trackers can be copied or pickled on newer Python versions. Several benchmark workflow issues were fixed.\n- **Documentation and Platform updates:** Docs clarify fine-tuning, inference, and precision behavior; Platform documentation covers relevance-based dataset sorting, email changes, and AI-assisted model comparison.\n\n## 🎯 Purpose & Impact\n- **Save storage and simplify sharing:** YOLO-World users can save and move custom-vocabulary checkpoints without carrying an unnecessary CLIP encoder.\n- **Trust results and continue training safely:** Validation matching and YOLOE resume fixes reduce misleading evaluation results and prevent trained heads from being lost.\n- **Get more dependable inference across devices:** SAM, ONNX, OpenVINO, image inputs, and video handling work more consistently across common workflows.\n- **Keep segmentation metrics stable:** Reverting the mask threshold avoids the measured mAP regression introduced by the earlier change.\n\n## What's Changed\n* Threshold rescaled segment val masks and keep saved video duration with vid_stride by @Nicholas022400701 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26416\n* Add Hailo-8 benchmarks picture to doc by @lakshanthad in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26615\n* Fix confidence-ordered validation matching for alternate targets by @Nikhi00718 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26616\n* Preserve ONNX input names and values in GPU binding by @aswanth-07 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26618\n* Fix empty MobileSAM masks in FP16 by computing LayerNorm2d with the native kernel by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26639\n* Revert segment val mask thresholding from #26416 by @Laughing-q in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26645\n* Make per-tracker track ID counters picklable on Python 3.14 by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26638\n* Reset SAM predictor state for every new source by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26644\n* Fix legacy precision flags, used models and repeat directory runs in benchmarks by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26640\n* Sync docs with recent precision, preprocessing, finetuning and Platform changes by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26633\n* Accept floating NumPy color images for grayscale models by @aswanth-07 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26632\n* Pin torch when auto-installing nvidia-modelopt for TensorRT 11 export by @Zephyr4772 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26624\n* Fix channel swap in ReID crops passed to embedding models by @cainiao33 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26628\n* Fix OpenVINO NPU batch and depth inference by @onuralpszr in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26641\n* Keep the fused YOLOE head when resuming or re-fine-tuning PE checkpoints by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26646\n* Preserve fractional and high FPS in saved videos and stream loaders by @Vaishnavi220506 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26627\n* Reseed Albumentations in each DataLoader worker by @8rulerstar in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26635\n* Preserve non-ASCII class names and paths in Windows logs by @Nikhi00718 in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26626\n* `ultralytics 8.4.176` Keep CLIP out of YOLO-World checkpoints after set_classes (328 MB → 26 MB) by @raimbekovm in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26647\n\n## New Contributors\n* @Zephyr4772 made their first contribution in https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/pull/26624\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/compare/v8.4.175...v8.4.176\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ultralytics/ultralytics/releases/410964449/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"mentions_count":11}]